# HPC scratch: job scripts and SLURM logs from cluster runs. Kept in-repo so
# they sit beside the work they describe, never committed -- they are noisy,
# machine-specific, and reference human-subjects audio paths. The README
# documents the convention so it survives a fresh clone.
/hpc/*
!/hpc/README.md

# Environment build recipes are source, not scratch. A global exclude on this
# machine ignores envs/ (the conda convention); the repo rule wins.
!/envs/
